From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Topher Campbell <chrs2021@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 02/22] cpufreq, cpuidle, devfreq, soc: mediatek: support the MT6771, SVS

mediatek-cpufreq and mtk-cci-devfreq gain MT6771 data (MediaTek's V5_T
table: A53 to 1989 MHz, A73 to 2106 MHz, CCI to 1196 MHz), cpufreq-dt
leaves the SoC to mediatek-cpufreq, and dt_idle_states can start every
idle state disabled (dt_idle_states.off=1) for bring-up. mtk-svs gains
the MT6771: the MT8183's banks for the CPUs and the CCI (MediaTek's EEM
for the MT6771 has the same detectors, efuse fields and limits), without
the GPU bank, whose thermal zone this SoC's thermal driver doesn't give.
---
 .../bindings/soc/mediatek/mtk-svs.yaml        |  1 +
 drivers/cpufreq/cpufreq-dt-platdev.c          |  1 +
 drivers/cpufreq/mediatek-cpufreq.c            | 65 +++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/cpuidle/dt_idle_states.c              | 11 ++++
 drivers/devfreq/mtk-cci-devfreq.c             |  9 +++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-svs.c                | 21 ++++++
 6 files changed, 108 insertions(+)

